# The runtime closure a user installs (plan D5, hash-pinned install
# path). This file holds ONLY what synthtwin needs to run: the
# development and build tooling lives in requirements-dev.in.
#
# The floors here must match the ones declared in pyproject.toml, and the
# ROOTS here must match them too: a package this file names is a package
# an institutional install puts on somebody's machine, whatever pandas
# happens to depend on. numpy left this list at Phase 1 review round 3
# for exactly that reason and returns at Phase 2 (plan P2-D8), now that
# the generator requires it by name rather than through pandas.
# tests/test_dependencies.py fails if either drifts.
--only-binary :all:
